## What changed

Same-speaker cue folding lands in the write path, so it applies to the persisted session bundle (the bilingual `.srt` transcript + the `.md` whose `#index` assist tags and `speakers` frontmatter stay keyed to the unchanged socket indices).

- **`server/session/srt.ts`** — two new helpers: `mergeCueText` stretches the last cue's end timestamp and space-joins the incoming text onto the source line (preserving a translation that already landed); `upsertTranslationLine` pushes a translation line or space-joins onto an existing one. [srt.ts:40-86](file://~/fluent-bench/runs/T6/ad-hoc/server/session/srt.ts)
- **`server/session/writer.ts`** — `SessionWriter.create` takes `opts.mergeMaxS` (default `0` = off). `appendSegment` folds a segment into the previous cue when the speaker label matches and the merged span `end_s - cueStart` stays under the threshold. Merged cues keep the first segment's cue number, so the `index+1` ↔ socket-index mapping used by translations and the backfill parser stays intact. `cueIndexFor` routes a folded index's translation into the right cue. [writer.ts:80-136](file://~/fluent-bench/runs/T6/ad-hoc/server/session/writer.ts)
- **`server/config.ts`** + **`.env.example`** — `TRANSCRIPT_MERGE_MAX_S`, coerce number, `0` disables, default `10`. <ref_snippet file="~/fluent-bench/runs/T6/ad-hoc/server/config.ts" line="22"/>
- **`server/session/manager.ts`** — passes `config.TRANSCRIPT_MERGE_MAX_S` into the writer. [manager.ts:186-188](file://~/fluent-bench/runs/T6/ad-hoc/server/session/manager.ts)

## Design notes

- Segments with no speaker label never fold — gluing unlabeled text isn't safe.
- Disabled path (`mergeMaxS: 0`) takes the exact original code path; the merge branch is skipped before any state changes.
- All file mutations serialize on the writer's existing queue, so a merge rewrite can't interleave with a translation splice.

